  "tagline": "Local-first TypeScript platform: SQLite on each device, end-to-end encrypted sync through relays.",
  "description": "Evolu is a local-first library and platform for TypeScript apps. Each device keeps its data in SQLite (WASM in browsers, native on React Native/Expo and Electron), queries it with type-safe SQL via Kysely, and syncs changes end-to-end encrypted through relays you can self-host, so the relay never sees plaintext. Identity is a mnemonic-based owner key rather than a server account. It suits privacy-sensitive apps where the server should never see user data; Trezor Suite uses it in production. The project is small and the platform still describes its general release as upcoming.",
